Topic 17 – Encapsulation
Objective: Data hiding, private variables, getters, setters and validation.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Employee Encapsulation	Create an Employee class with private ID, name and salary. Access them through getters and setters.
02	Student Encapsulation	Create a Student class with private marks. Use a setter to accept marks only between 0 and 100.
03	Bank Account	Create a private balance variable and expose deposit, withdrawal and balance retrieval methods.
04	Age Validation	Create a private age variable. Reject negative age values using a setter.
05	Password Encapsulation	Create a private password variable and provide a setter that validates minimum password length.
06	Read-Only Property	Create a class with private variables and only getters. Initialize values using a constructor.
07	Write-Only Property	Create a class with a private variable and setter only. Demonstrate controlled modification.
08	Encapsulation with Multiple Fields	Create an Employee class with private ID, name, department and salary. Validate each field through setters.
09	Data Hiding	Create a class containing private variables. Try accessing them directly from another class and observe the compiler error. Then access them through public methods.
10	QA Test Configuration	Create an encapsulated TestConfiguration class with private browser, URL and timeout fields. Provide validation through setters and retrieve the values through getters.